# Template for the SECRET file of one environment. Copy it, fill it in, never commit the copy:
#
#   ENV=qa    ->  .env.qa.local        bash / zsh : cp .env.local.example .env.qa.local
#   ENV=stage ->  .env.stage.local     PowerShell : Copy-Item .env.local.example .env.stage.local
#
# The name must match the environment: ENV=qa loads .env.qa and then .env.qa.local (a file called just ".env.local" is NOT
# read). .env.local, .env.*.local and .env are git-ignored. In CI use masked CI/CD variables instead of a file.
#
# Only secrets go here (see .env.example, entries marked "Secret: YES"). Everything else belongs in the committed .env.<name>.
# Values with # $ quotes or spaces must be wrapped in double quotes; a value with backslashes (DOMAIN\user) is safer unquoted.
# Remove the leading "# " of a line to use it and replace the placeholder with the real value.

# Password of the RDP login (REMOTE_ENABLED=true with REMOTE_AGENT_START=alternate-shell)
# REMOTE_RDP_PASSWORD="<rdp-password>"

# Connection string for database steps on the remote host
# REMOTE_DB_CONNECTION_STRING="<connection-string-as-the-host-uses-it>"

# Mail and file-transfer logins your own tests read through loadEnv()
# SMTP_PASS="<smtp-password>"
# SFTP_PASSWORD="<sftp-password>"
